evoort Street, from published descriptions; no photographs were available. Squared to the streets (the ground file has them axis-aligned here): the tall body of pale blue-grey steel panels facing the Hudson and West Street on the west, a glass ground floor and few windows, the north-light sawtooth roof over the top galleries; the east half lifted over the largo, the plaza at the foot of the High Line, and stepping down toward it in timber-decked terraces joined by outdoor stairs; the High Line on steel with its planting; Hudson River Park; low brick buildings of the Meatpacking District round it. Guessed: the heights (about 45 m), the terrace levels, the column positions under the cantilever, the neighbours."}